IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cda-nouns`

-- Criminal Damage Act 1971, section 4: PUNISHMENT OF OFFENCES.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Written from the text alone.
--
-- Section 4 states a CEILING, not a tariff: "liable to imprisonment for life" and
-- "liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years". Nothing here says
-- what sentence a court passes. The ceilings are stated only "on conviction on
-- indictment"; the text says nothing about summary conviction, so that mode of
-- conviction answers with an explicit "not stated" value and not with a number.
-- The penalties come from this text alone; no sentencing law from anywhere else.

§ `Section 4 -- Punishment of offences`

§§ `The modes of conviction and the ceilings`

DECLARE `Mode of conviction` IS ONE OF
    `on conviction on indictment`
    `on summary conviction`          -- the text of section 4 is silent about this mode

DECLARE `Maximum imprisonment` IS ONE OF
    `imprisonment for life`
    `imprisonment for a term not exceeding` HAS `years` IS A NUMBER
    `no maximum is stated in this text for that mode of conviction`
    `no offence under this Act, so no penalty`

§§ `4(1) -- life`

-- src:22 | 4 Punishment of offences.
-- src:23 | (1) A person guilty of arson under section 1 above or of an offence under section 1(2) above (whether arson or not) shall on conviction on indictment be liable to imprisonment for life.
@ref s 4(1) (src:22-23)
GIVEN offence IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 4(1) applies to` offence MEANS
    CONSIDER offence
    WHEN `an offence under section 1(1), not by fire` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `arson under section 1(1)` THEN TRUE                     -- "arson under section 1"
    WHEN `an offence under section 1(2), not by fire` THEN TRUE   -- "an offence under section 1(2) (whether arson or not)"
    WHEN `arson under section 1(2)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an offence under section 2(a)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under section 2(b)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under section 3(a)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under section 3(b)` THEN FALSE

§§ `4(2) -- ten years`

-- src:24 | (2) A person guilty of any other offence under this Act shall on conviction on indictment be liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years.
@ref s 4(2) (src:24)
GIVEN offence IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 4(2) applies to` offence MEANS
    -- "any other offence under this Act": every offence that section 4(1) does not name.
    NOT (`section 4(1) applies to` offence)

@ref s 4(2) (src:24)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ceiling in years in section 4(2)` MEANS 10

§§ `The most that can follow`

-- On conviction on indictment: life if any offence committed is one that section 4(1)
-- names, otherwise the ten years of section 4(2). The Act does not say that one act
-- committing two offences is punished once; this rule takes the heavier ceiling and
-- says nothing about cumulating anything.
@ref s 4(1), s 4(2) (src:24)
GIVEN offences IS A LIST OF Offence
GIVETH A `Maximum imprisonment`
`the heaviest ceiling on conviction on indictment among` offences MEANS
    IF any `section 4(1) applies to` offences
    THEN `imprisonment for life`
    ELSE `imprisonment for a term not exceeding` `the ceiling in years in section 4(2)`

@ref s 4(1), s 4(2) (src:24)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
      offences IS A LIST OF Offence
GIVETH A `Maximum imprisonment`
`the most that can follow` mode offences MEANS
    CONSIDER offences
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `no offence under this Act, so no penalty`
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY xs THEN
        CONSIDER mode
        WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN `the heaviest ceiling on conviction on indictment among` offences
        WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `no maximum is stated in this text for that mode of conviction`
